POLICY ARROW_MAIN SCORER : king-to-d1 / king-to-f1\nrows=[file,rank,0 x 416]
SCORER ARROW_MAIN POLICY : finite ordered f64 scores\ncanonical maximum
BRIDGE ARROW_MAIN ADMISSION : settle only / closed classical action\nwhite e1 to d1 or f1 / black pass
ADMISSION ARROW_MAIN NATIVE : same-open-state atomic pair\nnative income / bank reapplication
ADMISSION ARROW_MAIN BRIDGE : SCFEN / bank / raw engine results\nreport-only after action selection
POLICY ARROW_MAIN RESULT : validated settlement report\ntruth details never feed scoring
POLICY ARROW_ERROR FAILURE : invalid envelope / DTO mismatch\n30 s total includes 3 s reap reserve
BRIDGE ARROW_ERROR FAILURE : bounded stream or child failure\nno shell / eval / auto-install
ADMISSION ARROW_ERROR FAILURE : native admission or settlement failure

MAIN ARROW_MAIN CLI : run --config / suite --config --out\nreplay --record / smoke remains separate
CLI ARROW_MAIN SCHEDULE : closed SuiteSpec / arena-schedule-v1\nchecked product before allocation
SCHEDULE ARROW_MAIN RUN : MatchSpec / arena-match-v1\nexplicit fixture and per-seat policy seeds
CLI ARROW_MAIN RUN : one configured baseline match
RUN ARROW_MAIN CLIENT : session.start/open / select BOTH\nthen session.commit / close
CLIENT ARROW_MAIN WORKER : fixed Node --import tsx / no shell\n300 s total includes 3 s cleanup
WORKER ARROW_MAIN SESSION : private native lifecycle\nstale-context rejection
SESSION ARROW_MAIN FIXTURES : fixed native fixture / explicit bank
FIXTURES ARROW_MAIN NATIVE : native parse / validation
SESSION ARROW_MAIN NATIVE : isolated seats -> stable white/black merge\nendScTurn skipTurnStartChecks / native outcome
SESSION ARROW_MAIN RUN : one post-begin context + both views\nno per-window raw truth before selection
RUN ARROW_MAIN BASELINE : limited view only / no fixture or case ID\nseed goes only to explicit selector
BASELINE ARROW_MAIN CLIENT : PlanningOracle / <=8 pulls per RPC\n10 s absolute decision / no RPC renewal
WORKER ARROW_MAIN PLANNER : independent data-only planning contexts\n<=2 contexts / <=2063 cursors per view
PLANNER ARROW_MAIN BASELINE : nativeFailure / anchor / one-action cost\nonly core/planning-v1 + wire helpers
RUN ARROW_MAIN RECORD : selected queues / keys / diagnostics\nraw begin/resolve + SCFEN/bank/grants after choices
SESSION ARROW_ERROR FAILURE : native rejection ends run\nno pass rescue or mutation retry
CLIENT ARROW_ERROR FAILURE : byte / UTF-8 / ID / EOF / deadline failure\nretain prefix + unverified pending operation
SCHEDULE ARROW_MAIN REPLAY : independently verify every record\nretain each case's failure classification
CLI ARROW_MAIN REPLAY : bounded arena-run-v1 record\n<=16 MiB / no unchecked evaluation
REPLAY ARROW_MAIN CLIENT : replay.* namespace / regenerate policy\ncompare every native frame and selected key
WORKER ARROW_MAIN REPLAY_NATIVE : separate native replay lifecycle\nnever session.ts or commitWindow
REPLAY_NATIVE ARROW_MAIN FIXTURES : independently parse fixed SCFEN
REPLAY_NATIVE ARROW_MAIN NATIVE : independent projection / stage / reduction\ncompare raw payloads, banks and native outcomes
REPLAY ARROW_MAIN EVAL : private VerifiedRun capability\nonly after native AND policy agreement
SCHEDULE ARROW_MAIN EVAL : include explicit failed/unverified cases\nverified native rejection remains failed
REPLAY ARROW_ERROR FAILURE : tamper / missing frame / unknown tail\nverified prefix is not a verified terminal

note bottom of OBS
  Only visible board cells and the player's own
  resources cross the observation boundary,
  because private state would taint the proof.
  Hidden cells keep their positions while
  concealing enemy contents.
end note

note bottom of ADMISSION
  Stage both seats against the same open state,
  because sequential mutation would change
  simultaneous admission semantics. Keep bank
  state separate from the native snapshot and
  apply income only at native grant boundaries.
end note

note bottom of BRIDGE
  Each one-shot request reconstructs the same
  fixture rather than accepting caller state.
  This confines the bridge to compatibility
  checks and cannot establish a persistent
  match runner or a general replay protocol.
end note

note bottom of POLICY
  The policy receives only the limited
  observation before selecting an action, since
  full engine state would cross the boundary.
  Native settlement details become report data
  after selection and never feed the scorer.
end note

note bottom of SESSION
  Both seats select from the same native
  opening before private admission exposes
  truth. Stage requests independently, then
  merge in white-black order so one seat
  cannot alter the other's admission context.
end note

note right of SESSION
  Retain the mineral bank outside native
  transitions, because snapshots may omit
  stored resources. Grant income once at
  settlement; a terminal begin must never
  apply another income grant.
end note

note bottom of REPLAY_NATIVE
  Replaying the live commit path would repeat
  its mistakes instead of checking native
  results. Only replay may issue a private
  token after both native and policy checks
  agree, so evaluation cannot trust raw logs.
end note

note bottom of EVAL
  Native rejection remains a failed case even
  when independent replay confirms its cause.
  Keep every scheduled case in the denominator
  so verified terminals cannot hide failures
  or convert window limits into draws.
end note

legend bottom
  Native baseline source contract; current receipts live in native-runner.md.
  v1 smoke: two reconstructed one-shot calls / 30 s total includes 3 s reap.
  v1 Burn Flex f64 / 418 zero-padded rows / e1 -> d1 or f1 / black pass.
  v1 smoke mine observation cap 2 remains unchanged; v2 counts up to 3 entities.
  v2 request 64 KiB / reply 1 MiB / cumulative stderr 64 KiB; clear NODE_OPTIONS.
  v2 300 s total includes 3 s cleanup; decision 10 s absolute; xtask 600=597+3 s.
  Linux/Unix trusted built-in worker; no hostile-code sandbox or timing-fit claim.
  arena-policy-seeds-v1: base + (ordinal+1)*0x9e3779b9 + black*0x85ebca6b mod 2^32.
  Fixed fixtures do not use environmentSeed; case/fixture/seed metadata is host-only.
  Initial image is host-only; per-window truth follows both selections or stopped planning.
  Native outcome only; nonterminal host window limit is NOT a draw.
  scheduled = verified-terminal + verified-window-limited + failed/unverified.
  CLI config <=64 KiB / record <=16 MiB; private fresh outputs / no overwrite.
  fullRunner=true states capability, not verification, training or a learned scorer.
  No R4 economy/belief/features/calibration/readiness closure or pinned-54 win claim.
  Preserve legacy consumers/evidence; delete legacy LAST after final consumer parity.
endlegend
@enduml
